    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 45 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The redesign is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers, and moved every value that derived from the old identity onto the new one.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewrote to build `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n   - `REGION` derived from the postcode (postcode range preferred, city fallback, else `UNKNOWN`).\n   - `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (the telephone is the stored E.164-normalized value). Removed the now-unused `OwnerRepository` count logic.\n\n2. **`OwnerRegion.java`** (new) \u2014 a shared helper for region-from-postcode-or-city, used by both the code assignment and the locality fallback so the derivation stays single-sourced.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.deriveLocality`** \u2014 now extracts the region from the `<REGION>-` prefix of the `customerCode` (the region-and-hash identity), falling back to live postcode/city derivation only for legacy owners without such a code.\n\n4. Values that already read `customerCode` needed no logic change and now automatically reflect the new identity:\n   - **Membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`)\n   - **Luhn check digit** (`luhnCheckDigit` over the code's digits)\n   - **Create audit line** (logs `customerCode`)\n\n   I updated their doc comments/examples to reflect the new format.\n\nVerified: the seven directly-affected checkpoints (Cp09, Cp14, Cp16, Cp21, Cp30, Cp31, Cp32) and the full 45-test suite are green.",
